	<<link [[Next|Mansion Skyscraper Dress]]>><<npc Avery>><<person1>><</link>>
	<br>

<</if>>

:: Mansion Ruin
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<effects>>

You approach the burnt out ruin of Avery's mansion. One gate stands open, the other lies detached from the wall. The garden grows wild.
<br><br>

<<if $museumAntiques.antiques.antiquegoldmask is "notFound">>
	<<link [[Search the rubble (1:00)|Mansion Ruin Search]]>><<pass 60>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Leave (0:05)|Danube Street]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Ruin Search
<<effects>>

You clamber over the rubble, looking for anything of interest. You notice a yellow glint in the ash.
<br><br>
<<if $museumAntiques.antiques.antiquegolddagger is "notFound">>
	<<museumAntiqueStatus "antiquegolddagger" "found">>
	<<set $antiquemoney += 4000>>
	You dig out the object. It's a gold dagger, a survivor from Avery's display room. It would be worth something to a museum.
	<br><br>
<<elseif $museumAntiques.antiques.antiquegoldamulet is "notFound">>
	<<museumAntiqueStatus "antiquegoldamulet" "found">>
	<<set $antiquemoney += 4000>>
	You dig out the object. It's a gold amulet, old and burned, but still valuable to a museum.
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	You dig out the object. It's a gold mask. It looks very valuable. A museum would be interested.
	<br><br>
	You don't think there's anything else to find here.
	<br><br>
	<<museumAntiqueStatus "antiquegoldmask" "found">>
	<<set $antiquemoney += 12000>>
<</if>>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Ruin]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Fire
<<set $location to "avery_mansion">><<effects>>

You approach Avery's flaming mansion. Two fire engines a parked outside. The firefighters themselves stand at attention, equipment ready, but unused.
<br><br>

<<link [[Ask why they're not putting it out|Mansion Fire Ask]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave (0:05)|Danube Street]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Fire Ask
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Excuse me," you say. "Why aren't you putting out the fire?"
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"I trust there's a reason you lot are just stood around," you say.
<<else>>
	"Why aren't you putting out the fire?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<generate1>><<person1>>
"Too dangerous," a <<person>> dressed as a firefighters says. "The building's made of, er, exotic materials, and we've confirmed there's no one inside. We're keeping an eye on it to make sure it doesn't spread elsewhere. That's the important thing. Been good so far. Suspiciously good, if you ask me."
<br><br>

<<He>> turns back to the flames.
<br><br>

<<link [[Leave (0:05)|Danube Street]]>><<endevent>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Robin
<<effects>>

On the other side of the gate, staring up at the mansion in awe, is Robin.
<br><br>

<<He>> tears <<his>> gaze away as you approach, and smiles at you. "I didn't expect it to be so," <<he>> pauses. "Big." <<He>> reaches into <<his>> bag, produces a folder, and pushes it through the bars.
<br><br>

"Just a small gift from everyone," Robin says as you open it. It's full of letters, some long, some short, all thanking you, and wishing you the best. Some are illustrated with drawings of various complexity. There are many, some are even from ex-residents, much older than you.<<gstress>><<stress 6>><<ltrauma>><<trauma 6>>
<br><br>

<<link [["Thank Robin, and invite " + $NPCList[0].pronouns.him + "in"|Mansion Robin Invite]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Just thank Robin|Mansion Robin Thank]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Robin Invite
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"It's wonderful," you say. "Thank you. Would you like to come in?"
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"I'm glad people miss me," you say. "Come inside."
<<else>>
	"Thank you," you say. "Would you like to come in?"
<</if>>
<br><br>

Robin takes another glance at the mansion, then steps back in trepidation. "I can't. It would feel wrong." <<He>> flashes a smile. "I'll be happy to see you at the orphanage. It's good you're still nearby, and not further way."
<br><br>

<<He>> puts <<his>> arms through the bars to hug you as best <<he>> can, then <<he>> walks down the boulevard.
<br><br>

You look again at the folder Robin gave you. What do you do with it?
<br><br>

<<link [[Keep it|Mansion Robin Keep]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Throw it away|Mansion Robin Throw]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Robin Thank
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"It's wonderful," you say. "Thank you."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"I'm glad people miss me," you say.
<<else>>
	"Thank you," you say. "It means a lot to me."
<</if>>
<br><br>

Robin smiles, then reaches through the bars to attempt a hug. "I'm glad you're not far away, and can still visit the orphanage," <<he>> says. <<He>> turns around, and walks down the boulevard.
<br><br>

You look again at the folder Robin gave you. What do you do with it?
<br><br>

<<link [[Keep it|Mansion Robin Keep]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Throw it away|Mansion Robin Throw]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Robin Keep
<<effects>>

<<set $avery_mansion.folder to 1>>
You take the folder inside, to the bedroom, and place it in the drawyer by your bedside.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Bedroom]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Robin Throw
<<effects>>

You go to the kitchen, and throw it with the rest of the rubbish. Avery probably wouldn't like you reading it, anyway.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Kitchen]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Folder
<<effects>>

You sit on the bed and flip through the folder, stopping to read the letters as takes your fancy. You don't remember all the events portrayed, but you don't doubt they're true.
<br><br>

Satisfied for now, you return the folder to bedside cabinet.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Bedroom]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Folder Avery
<<effects>>

You sit on the bed and search the bedside cabinet for the folder from the orphanage, <span class="red">but it isn't there.</span>
<br><br>
Avery enters, and spares you a glance as <<he>> walks to the wardrobe.

<<if C.npc.Avery.rage gte random(20, 100) and $averyragerevealed gte 1>>
	"I threw that thing away," <<he>> says. "You kept staring at it. It's annoying."
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Search the bin|Mansion Folder Rage Search]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Get angry|Mansion Folder Rage Angry]]>><<npcincr Avery rage 1>><</link>><<garage>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Silently accept it|Mansion Folder Rage Silent]]>><<npcincr Avery dom 1>><<npcincr Avery love 1>><</link>><<gdom>><<glove>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	"Looking for the folder?" <<he>> asks. "I threw it out. I can't abide clutter."
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Search the bin|Mansion Folder Search]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Get angry|Mansion Folder Angry]]>><<npcincr Avery rage 1>><</link>><<garage>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Silently accept it|Mansion Folder Silent]]>><<npcincr Avery dom 1>><<npcincr Avery love 1>><</link>><<gdom>><<glove>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Mansion Folder Search
<<effects>>

You walk over to the bin. It's empty.
<br><br>
"Don't bother," Avery says, emerging from the wardrobe with a fresh pair of shoes. "It's not here, and would have been shredded by now anyway."
<br><br>

<<link [[Search the bin|Mansion Folder Search]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Silently accept it|Mansion Folder Silent]]>><<npcincr Avery dom 1>><<npcincr Avery love 1>><</link>><<gdom>><<glove>>
<br>

:: Mansion Folder Angry
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
	"That was very unkind of you," you say.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Maybe I should throw away your things," you say. "See how you like it."
<<else>>
	"It wasn't yours to throw away," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Avery shrugs. "I thought you were done with it. You've looked at it enough. Besides, the sooner you forget about that vulgar place, the better."
<br><br>

Avery emerges from the wardrobe, a fresh pair of shoes in hand, and walks away.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Mansion Folder Silent
<<effects>>

You sit, silent, and stare at your lap. "Don't look so glum," Avery says. "The sooner you put that vulgar place behind you, the better." <<He>> emerges from the wardrobe with a pair of fresh shoes in hand, and walks away.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Mansion Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

